<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Deliberately EMPTY. It carries no settings, and it must stay that way.

  Between 2026-10-27 and 2026-10-29 this folder shipped a web.config that set a .dmg
  MIME type. IIS could not apply it, and every URL under /download_app_files/ -- the
  .exe, both .dmg, the folder itself -- answered "500 Internal server error". Removing
  the file from the repository did not help the server: copying a new build over the
  deployed folder never deletes the file that is already there, so the broken one stayed
  and every installer download failed ("Site wasn't available").

  This file exists so that the next copy of the build OVERWRITES the broken one with
  something IIS can always read. An empty <configuration> cannot fail.

  Put no <system.webServer>, <staticContent>, <rewrite> or <handlers> here. The .dmg
  MIME type is set once, at the site level, in IIS Manager (docs/Desktop_Release_Runbook.md
  section 8.7). frontend/src/api/__tests__/downloadFolder.test.ts fails if this file
  gains any setting.
-->
<configuration>
</configuration>
